schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Purpose-People-Place-Process-Practice (5P gathering framework)
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A five-element design framework for gatherings — a specific purpose, a
    deliberate guest list, a matched space, a designed process arc (opening/
    body/closing), and post-gathering practice (follow-through) — treating
    every gathering as an intentional design challenge rather than a default
    meetup script.
  source_traditions:
    - Priya Parker, "The Art of Gathering" (Riverhead Books, 2018)
    - Adrienne Maree Brown, "Emergent Strategy" (AK Press, 2017)
    - Open Civics Framework
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Applied to four local-node gathering formats (Onboarding, Governance,
    Trust-Building, Learning) as the structural template organizers are
    instructed to work through before hosting.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - World Café
    - Fishbowl
    - Open Space Technology
    - Liberating Structures (33 facilitation methods)
    - Circle Practice (talking-piece format)
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      "Purpose is not topic" — the article is explicit that "to learn about
      Web3" is a topic, not a purpose; a purpose states what will be
      different afterward.
    - >-
      "Agreements are mutual, rules are imposed" — the article deliberately
      avoids "ground rules" language in the Opening step.
  tensions:
    - >-
      Small-group-first, curated-guest-list design guidance vs. open/
      inclusive-by-default community norms.
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    The article attributes Circle Practice's talking-piece format and the
    small-group-before-large-group decision pattern to "many African and
    Indigenous traditions" and "many East African communities" in passing,
    secondary-source, non-attributed-to-a-specific-community language.
    Treating that as settled ethnography rather than a broad-strokes,
    unverified attribution risks flattening living traditions into a
    facilitation technique. See accompanying public-use-boundary.
  high_risk: true
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/gatherings-pattern.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
